jimaku contains code extracted and rewritten from rokrokss/shizue
(https://github.com/rokrokss/shizue), commit c2ebc51 (v0.3.17).

Sources:
- src/core/captions.ts   … how json3 captions are read and how endTime is trimmed
                           (src/lib/captionInjector.tsx)
- src/core/tracks.ts     … the ytInitialPlayerResponse regex, how the caption track is chosen,
                           and how the timedtext URL is built (src/lib/youtube.ts)
- src/content/youtube.ts … how the player's timedtext request is caught, and how the CC button
                           is used to make the player send one (src/lib/youtube.ts)
- src/core/bridge.ts, src/page/player-bridge.ts
                         … how to talk to a MAIN world script through CustomEvent (with the
                           detail as a JSON string) (src/entrypoints/youtube-player-hook.content.ts,
                           src/lib/youtubeCaption/hookProtocol.ts)
- src/core/chatgpt-auth.ts
                         … the Sign in with ChatGPT flow: authorize parameters, callback checks,
                           token exchange and refresh, ID token checks, revocation
                           (src/lib/chatgptAuth.ts)
- src/core/chatgpt-responses.ts
                         … error handling, the model catalog and the Responses API event stream
                           parser (src/lib/chatgptResponses.ts)
- src/background/main.ts … catching the loopback callback with a declarativeNetRequest session
                           rule (src/services/background/chatgpt.ts)
- src/callback/main.ts   … the callback page that hands the query string to the background
                           (src/entrypoints/chatgpt-callback/main.ts)

src/core/translate.ts used to use Shizue's approach of splitting in half and retrying when the
line count doesn't match (src/services/background/translationHandler.ts). It now retries only
the missing lines using numbered lines instead, and contains no Shizue code.

